WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.578
Medicare Advantage, Part C, lets Dennis receive his Medicare benefits through a

00:00:05.578 --> 00:00:10.692
private plan that Medicare pays a fixed monthly amount per member.

00:00:10.692 --> 00:00:14.410
To join he must have Parts A and

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.129
B and live in the plan’s service area.

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:23.707
The plan must cover everything Original Medicare covers, except hospice, which Original

00:00:23.707 --> 00:00:29.285
Medicare continues to pay, and most plans include Part D drug coverage

00:00:29.285 --> 00:00:33.934
and extras such as dental, vision, hearing and fitness benefits.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:38.118
Dennis keeps paying his Part B premium, and the

00:00:38.118 --> 00:00:41.836
plan may charge its own premium, often zero.

00:00:41.836 --> 00:00:46.020
The plan’s rules, networks and cost sharing replace Medicare’s.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.761
Advantage plans come in the designs you know.

00:00:49.761 --> 00:00:53.502
HMOs require a primary care physician and referrals

00:00:53.502 --> 00:00:57.242
and cover nothing out of network except emergencies.

00:00:57.242 --> 00:01:00.983
PPOs pay more in network and less out.

00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:07.062
Private fee-for-service plans let members see any provider who accepts the plan’s terms.

00:01:07.062 --> 00:01:10.803
Special needs plans serve people with specific conditions,

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:14.544
those in institutions or those also on Medicaid.

00:01:14.544 --> 00:01:19.220
Unlike Original Medicare, every Advantage plan has an annual out-of-pocket

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.896
maximum for Part A and B services, a real protection.

00:01:23.896 --> 00:01:29.974
Plans may not deny enrollment for health conditions; ESRD patients may also enroll.

00:01:29.974 --> 00:01:32.780
Medicare publishes star ratings for quality.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:37.951
Dennis may join an Advantage plan during his initial Medicare enrollment period.

00:01:37.951 --> 00:01:43.983
Each year the annual election period runs October 15 through December 7, when anyone

00:01:43.983 --> 00:01:50.016
may join, switch or drop an Advantage or Part D plan for January 1.

00:01:50.016 --> 00:01:54.756
A Medicare Advantage open enrollment period from January 1 through March

00:01:54.756 --> 00:01:59.496
31 lets a current Advantage member switch once to another Advantage

00:01:59.496 --> 00:02:04.236
plan or return to Original Medicare with a Part D plan.

00:02:04.236 --> 00:02:10.268
Special enrollment periods follow moves, loss of other coverage, Medicaid changes and plan terminations.

00:02:10.268 --> 00:02:15.870
A member cannot hold a Medicare supplement policy while in an Advantage plan.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:21.487
Part D is optional outpatient drug coverage sold by private insurers, either as a

00:02:21.487 --> 00:02:27.104
stand-alone prescription drug plan paired with Original Medicare or built into an Advantage plan.

00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:32.320
Each plan has a formulary, a list of covered drugs arranged in tiers

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.134
with different cost sharing, and may use prior authorization and step therapy.

00:02:37.134 --> 00:02:41.949
Enrollment windows match Part B’s initial period and the annual election period.

00:02:41.949 --> 00:02:47.566
The standard benefit has a deductible, 615 dollars in 2026, then cost sharing of

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:53.183
about 25 percent until the member’s out-of-pocket spending reaches the annual cap, 2,100 dollars

00:02:53.183 --> 00:02:58.800
in 2026, after which covered drugs cost nothing for the rest of the year.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.494
Dennis can avoid a Part D late penalty by enrolling when he is first

00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:08.188
eligible or keeping drug coverage that is at least as good as Part D.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:11.541
If he goes 63 days in a row without that

00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:14.894
coverage after his initial enrollment period, a penalty can apply.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.576
For each full uncovered month, it is one

00:03:17.576 --> 00:03:19.924
percent of the national base beneficiary premium.

00:03:19.924 --> 00:03:23.612
He generally pays it as long as he has Part D.

00:03:23.612 --> 00:03:27.300
People who qualify for Extra Help do not owe this penalty.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.318
The Medicare Prescription Payment Plan is separate: it lets

00:03:30.318 --> 00:03:33.000
members spread their drug costs across the year.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.247
Dennis has two coherent choices.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:39.742
Road one: Original Medicare, a Medicare supplement policy to fill

00:03:39.742 --> 00:03:44.237
the deductibles and coinsurance, and a stand-alone Part D plan.

00:03:44.237 --> 00:03:47.833
He may see any provider who takes Medicare,

00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:51.429
nationwide, with predictable costs and higher monthly premiums.

00:03:51.429 --> 00:03:56.823
Road two: a Medicare Advantage plan, usually with drug coverage and extras,

00:03:56.823 --> 00:04:01.767
lower premiums, a network and referral rules, and an out-of-pocket maximum.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:06.711
He may switch between roads during election periods, but returning to

00:04:06.711 --> 00:04:11.656
a supplement later may require medical underwriting outside Maryland’s protected windows.

00:04:11.656 --> 00:04:16.600
Lesson 44 explains the supplement side; Lesson 45 explains Maryland’s protections.
